# Closed objects every 3006.102.10 model shares (one blob on RT-BE96U, RT-BE86U, RT-BE88U and
# GT-BE98_PRO), which the models built with an older ASUS GPL drop take from canon as well.
# ci/container_build.sh (phase common-blobs) requires each listed file of GT-BE98, GT-BE19000, BQ16
# and BQ16_PRO to be byte-identical to canon's copy after their platform archive is unpacked.
#
# Format: <kind> <path> [-MODEL ...]
#   prebuild  path under release/src/router with MODEL standing for the model's directory name;
#             compared with the RT-BE96U copy.
#   sysdep    path under release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/router-sysdep.<model>/; compared with
#             router-sysdep.rt-be96u. The Wi-Fi driver / dataplane set (hnd_extra, wl, dhd, wlconf,
#             eapd, wlc_types.h, bp3, debug_monitor) is NOT listed: it stays with the model's drop.
#   -MODEL    the model keeps its own copy (the BQ16s' libamas-utils.so exports functions their
#             closed AiMesh objects need that the newer library does not).
# rc/prebuild/MODEL/mswan-broadcom.o is omitted: MULTISERVICE_WAN only, which none of the four sets.
prebuild aaews/prebuild/MODEL/aae_ipc.o
prebuild aaews/prebuild/MODEL/aaews
prebuild aaews/prebuild/MODEL/mastiff
prebuild ahs/prebuild/MODEL/ahs
prebuild amas-utils/prebuild/MODEL/amas-utils-cli -BQ16 -BQ16_PRO
prebuild amas-utils/prebuild/MODEL/amas-utils.h
prebuild amas-utils/prebuild/MODEL/libamas-utils.so -BQ16 -BQ16_PRO
prebuild asd/prebuild/MODEL/asd
